// @error a `type` declaration may not take the built-in type name `u8`
// D1585, the OWNER RULING (2026-09-04) — a user type named after a built-in type is refused
// at its DECLARATION, exported or not, so no importer's use of it ever arises. This entry
// never mentions `u8`; the program is refused for what the dependency declares.
//
// This file was D1571's CONTROL and asserted the opposite: `export type u8` renamed to
// `u8$mN` across the merge, shadowed the storage type here, and printed `5`. D1571 kept that
// deliberately — its narrow rule was "a built-in type name is renamed in TYPE position only
// by a `type` row" — and filed the dodge as an open observation, because closing it takes a
// running program away. The owner ruled it should be taken away: a user type that shadows
// `i32` / `f64` / `u8` has no upside and confuses at a distance.
//
// `modules/builtin-type-name-export/` is the half that MUST stay legal — a VALUE may take a
// built-in type name, which is D1571's actual rule and is untouched here.
import { ping } from "./lib"

print(ping())
